      "hints": [
        "Substitute $f(x)$ into $g(x) = 2x + 5$: $gf(x) = -4x^2 + 24x - 1$.",
        "Solve $-4x^2 + 24x - 1 + 1 = 0 \\implies -4x(x - 6) = 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Form the composite function $gf(x) = g(f(x))$:\n$$gf(x) = 2(-2x^2 + 12x - 3) + 5 = -4x^2 + 24x - 6 + 5 = -4x^2 + 24x - 1$$",
        "Substitute into the equation $gf(x) + 1 = 0$:\n$$(-4x^2 + 24x - 1) + 1 = 0 \\implies -4x^2 + 24x = 0$$",
